To integrate the RNFR (Rename From) and NOOP (No Operation) commands into the sequence of client requests you provided, we need to determine logical places for these commands.

The RNFR command is typically used before a rename operation (RNTO - Rename To), so it would make sense to place it before any directory or file manipulation commands. The NOOP command can be placed anywhere, but it is often used as a keep-alive command in FTP sessions.

Here’s a modified version of your sequence with RNFR and NOOP added:

```
USER ubuntu
PASS ubuntu
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,132,209
LIST
NOOP
MKD test
RNFR test
QUIT
```

In this modified sequence:
- I added the NOOP command after the LIST command to keep the session active.
- I added the RNFR command before the QUIT command, assuming you intend to rename a directory or file named "test" before ending the session. 

If you have a specific context for the RNFR command or if you want the NOOP command in a different location, please let me know!

